# gate/lower/fallback.baseline — measured pins for gate/lower/fallback.sh.
#
# One row per SHC transfer subject: the exact number of
# `duo_fatal("unlowered native call")` sites that `idol dump-c <file> --lib`
# emits, or REFUSED when the route fails closed instead.
#
# Measured at dec7d509 (origin/main) with ./zig-out/bin/idol built from that
# revision. Build mode is not the sensitive axis: a ReleaseFast build of the
# same revision reproduces every row exactly. REVISION is -- the tracked stale
# out/bin/idol reports lib/compiler/parser.id as REFUSED where this revision
# reports 291, and the gate calls that a CLASS CHANGE rather than agreeing.
#
# These are not a budget. Every nonzero row is a body the SHC transfer route
# replaces with a runtime abort while exiting 0, and every one of them must
# reach 0 or REFUSED before the source it names can execute inside a compiler.
# The three on lib/compiler/token_view.id are the GAP-134 parser-slice
# prerequisite; the 291 on lib/compiler/parser.id are why that file is a
# shadow authority and not a transfer candidate.
0	lib/compiler/application.id
0	lib/compiler/arm64.id
REFUSED	lib/compiler/arm64check.id
17	lib/compiler/bind.id
0	lib/compiler/comptime.id
REFUSED	lib/compiler/emit_c.id
0	lib/compiler/fmt.id
5	lib/compiler/graph.id
0	lib/compiler/lexer.id
0	lib/compiler/macho.id
0	lib/compiler/monolith.id
291	lib/compiler/parser.id
0	lib/compiler/profile.id
0	lib/compiler/reader.id
0	lib/compiler/record.id
3	lib/compiler/rewrite.id
REFUSED	lib/compiler/symbol.id
REFUSED	lib/compiler/token.id
3	lib/compiler/token_view.id
0	lib/token/classify.id
0	lib/token/grammarrole.id
